<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29799" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mucro</span></b> , ōnis, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a sharp point</i> or
				<i>edge;</i> esp., <i>the point of a
				sword, the sword's point</i> (class.; cf.: acies, cuspis).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mucro falcis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					4, 25, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 8,
					3, 4, § 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">folii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 10, 16, § 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crystalli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
				37</span></i>
			,  2, 9, § 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">26: cultri,</span>”
				<i>edge</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					14, 216</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medio jugulaberis ensis,</span>”
				<i>sword's point</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 484</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coruscus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 2, 333</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A sword</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nisi mucrones militum tremere voltis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 14, 3, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortalis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 12, 740</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A point, extremity, end</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose), <i><span class="en">Lucr. 2,
			520</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">faucium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 13, 15, § 38</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>edge, point,
				sharpness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">censorii stili,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Clu. 44, 123</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tribunicius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Leg. 3, 9, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">defensionis tuae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Caecin. 29, 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ingenii,</span>”
				<i>sharpness</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 5, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
